From 36ff5239c0c8c1500b2f76089790845cd57983fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: monomorphise a GAT's bounds with the projection's
 arguments when reached through another bound

hybrid-array 0.4.12 (rars 0.9.4) lib.rs:232, in `Array::concat<N>`:

    type ArrayType<T>: .. + IntoIterator<Item = T>;            // ArraySize
    type IntoIter = <U::ArrayType<T> as IntoIterator>::IntoIter; // IntoIterator for Array
    for (val, dst) in self.into_iter().zip(left) { .. }

`.zip` needs `<<U as ArraySize>::ArrayType<T> as IntoIterator>::IntoIter:
Iterator`. find_trait_impls_bound finds it through `U: ArraySize` and the
GAT's bound `IntoIterator<Item = T>`. It monomorphised that bound with no
method-level params, but a GAT's own parameters are numbered in that slot,
so the GAT's `T` hit "BUG: src/hir_typeck/common.cpp:692: Method
parameters were not expected (got T/*M:0*/)". Had a slot been there,
`T/*M:0*/` would have become the caller's first method generic (`N` here).

Pass the projection's arguments (`assoc_info->params`), as the static.cpp
copy of this code already does since 0103 and as helpers' method lookup
through ATY bounds does. The `Unsize` checks on associated type bounds in
helpers.cpp and static.cpp had the same `nullptr` and get the same fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
